  Gaps in the harness reported by the agent
  - build/local_install.sh: is_installed() checks only that config_inc.php and tests/bootstrap.php exist and that mantis_project_table has rows. It does not check that the API token in tests/bootstrap.php matches the database. Here the DB had been installed again (17:59 UTC) after the files were written (17:55 UTC). The token then resolved to the anonymous user, and every REST test (also the existing RestIssueTest) failed with 403 'User does not have access right to report issues'. make dev and make check do not detect this. The install could check the token with GET /api/rest/users/me.
  - compose.yaml: The compose project name is fixed to 'mantisbt', so every copy or worktree of this repository on the same machine shares one MySQL container and database. A setup or reset in one copy breaks the token of another copy without any message. That is the most likely cause of the reset above, but I could not find which process did it.
  - docs/local-dev.md: Common problems does not list 'REST/SOAP tests fail with 403 Access Denied / token resolves to anonymous' with 'make reset-db' as the fix. It covers only 'token CI_PHPUnit already exists'.
  - AGENTS.md: It does not say how to run one REST test class: you need a server on :8080 (make dev in the background) and then vendor/bin/phpunit <file>. The table says rest needs make dev running, but not that make dev runs in the foreground and must be started in the background or in a second shell.
  - docs/harness/log.md: It mentions the implicitly nullable parameter but not that the renamed class also had non-static data providers. Under PHPUnit 10 with failOnAllIssues these are deprecations that fail the run, so renaming the file and fixing ?int alone would have broken make check.

